-- A rule with a word between its inputs is one definition and has no clauses.
-- Two lines written in its form, with a literal for an input, were read as a
-- group of clauses defining a rule named like its own input, and refused in
-- twelve messages, three of them with no location. They are refused once, at
-- the first line.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
c `costs` 0 MEANS 0
c `costs` n MEANS n

#EVAL Red `costs` 0
#EVAL Green `costs` 5
